/*  popScratch -- THE CLASSIFIER'S OWN POP. 30 dumpRulePlans calls: the JSON
    family, the two ladder scaffolds, a SPREAD of the real bootstrap grammar,
    and one deliberate NON-rule. The ladder targets cannot test the classifier
    (Scaf/ScafA/ScafB reach two kinds of five and never carry an unmaterialised
    term), so this is the POP it otherwise lacks. Every term must come back with
    the same plan node or the same refusal. Diff against genLadder/census.target.

    ⚠⚠ RENAMED FROM `censusScratch` 2026-08-05 (Tony), AND THE RENAME IS THE
    FINDING. This file is a hand-listed SAMPLE -- its own header always said "a
    spread" -- but the name said CENSUS, and a census is an enumeration. That
    misreading cost real ground: the grammar campaign opened believing "the
    census asserts 30 rules" described COVERAGE of the grammar. The measured
    population is 78 (Grokking: 60 rule members + 18 rule attributes), of which
    this file touches 18. The fixture is well built for its actual job; only its
    name was wrong, and its own author misread it.

    ⚠ HEADER DRIFT FIXED IN THE SAME TOUCH: this said "27 rules" while making 30
    calls. The last three -- debug, DEBUG, InvokE -- were appended without the
    count moving. A number written without re-counting is a lie in the ledger.

    ⚠ `debug` IS A DELIBERATE NEGATIVE CONTROL, not a typo for DEBUG. It must
    come back REFUSED ("not a rule; locate finds a non-rule in registry
    Keywords", census.target:161-162) while DEBUG -- the real rule, the very next
    call -- plans or refuses on its merits. Do not "fix" the case.  */
register(Ladder);
